3 DATE 29 December 1928
3 TEXT &quot;To Menno (Duerksen) from Uncle J. F. Duerksen - Esther (Esther Ruth Duerksen 1904-1998)&quot;
3 WWW http://person.ancestry.com/tree/52881559/person/13422621104/gallery
2 NOTE The source from which all Duerksen/Dirksen family histories prior to  1995 were drawn. In June 1995 California Mennonite Historical Society Bulletin #32 was published revealing many inaccuracies in the 1928 Duerksen Family History.
1 NOTE * Birth Source:  John Funk Duerksen&apos;s 1928 papers, also called the &quot;Duerksen book&quot;, in the Marcellus Duerksen Folder, Hiebert Library, Fresno. Inaccuracies revealed by Alan Peters in Mennonite Historical Society Bulletin No. 32 Jun
2 CONC e 1995.
2 CONT * Death Source:  John Funk Duerksen&apos;s 1928 papers.
2 CONT * Marriage Source: www.dakotadirksens.com
2 CONT * Notes:  John Funk Duerksen&apos;s 1928 papers call this man Johann but the 1835 Molotschna Census says his son&apos;s father was a Kornelius. John Funk Duerksen&apos;s 1928 papers also identify this man with David Duerksen (#14628) whom Duerkse
2 CONC n also called Johann. It may be that John Funk Duerksen combined the life events of two brothers, David Duerksen (#14628, born in 1761) and Johann Duerksen (#I14929, born about 1766). Circumstantial evidence supporting such a sibling relationship i
2 CONC ncludes the fact that one year after David (#14628) died in 1818, his son Cornelius emigrated with Johann to Russia where they became two of the sixteen founding families of Alexanderthal.
2 CONT    
2 CONT This man may be the Kornelius Duerksen, son of Cornelius Duerksen, who was baptized in 1754 as per the Montau baptism records.
