2 CONT Birth Source: California Online Death Records Death Source: California Online Death Records Notes: He was an Adventist. Listed in Adventist obit. list b3-28-1883 d3-24-1960. He was converted at the age of 8, baptized and united with the Richville
2 CONC , North Dakota SDA church at the age of 14. Attended bible schools at Columbia SD and Jamestown ND. Became a Bible instructor at Fargo ND in 1904. Elected a church elder in spring 1917, at Woodworth, North Dakota. He was married by his brother Henr
2 CONC y J. Dirksen. He was an Adventist minister in Woodworth, North Dakota. granted a ministerial License July 1, 1919 at the Jamestown North Dakota Camp meeting. He began ministerial labors at Diesem, N. Dakota. He was ordained June 24, 1921 in Manda
2 CONC n at the campground in the German Tabernacle. Retired from ministry as Associate Pastor of College View Church Lincoln NB 1953. Came to California in 1956.
