1 NOTE    
2 CONT Lawrence Beckner was born about 1733 in Germany.  Lawrence died 1802 in Boutetourt County, Virginia.  He married Susanna about 1756 in Pennsylvania.  She was born about 1740.  Susanna died before 1802. They had six children.
2 CONT    
2 CONT Lawrence is not found on any immigration records, as he would have been seven years old at the time of their arrival in 1740, and children had to be fifteen years old to be listed separately from their parents.
2 CONT    
2 CONT Lawrence is found on the 1762, 1772, 1779-1783 Tax Lists for York County, Pennsylvania.  He is also shown on the 1781 Muster List in York County. The year 1762 appears to be the earliest that the Beckner name is found in this part of Pennsylvania
2 CONC .  IT is assumed that the family resided in the Philadelphia area (their port city) until about 1760.  In 1770, Lawrence&apos;s name, as well as the names of Daniel, NIcholas, and Johan Nicholas, were found on the rolls of the Great Conewago Church
2 CONC .
2 CONT    
2 CONT The first deed found for Lawrence in Virginia is in Botetourt County (Deed Bk 3, pg 399) and is dated 8 August 1786.  It records the purchase of 200 acres on Looney&apos;s Mill Creek for four hundred British Pounds Sterling.  Lawrence also appear
2 CONC s on an 1800 Botetourt Tax List as being over 21 and owning no horses.  Lawrence&apos;s will, written 21 May 1802 (Will Book B, pg 23), and probated at the October court that year gives his land (72 acres) to his son Daniel and (105 acres) to his s
2 CONC on Jonathan. To the remainder of his children, Jacob Beckner, John Beckner, Elizabeth Simmons and Susan Garman, he bequeathed money (expressed in British Pounds).  The will was probated October, 1802
2 CONT    
2 CONT *Taken from book &quot;Beckners in America The First 250 Years&quot;, compiled by Brenda Cook Beckner &amp; Barbara Roland Beckner, published by Gateway Press, Inc., Baltimore, MD. 1996, page 1
2 CONT    
