2 CONC s on an 1800 Botetourt Tax List as being over 21 and owning no horses.  Lawrence&apos;s will, written 21 May 1802 (Will Book B, pg 23), and probated at the October court that year gives his land (72 acres) to his son Daniel and (105 acres) to his s
2 CONC on Jonathan. To the remainder of his children, Jacob Beckner, John Beckner, Elizabeth Simmons and Susan Garman, he bequeathed money (expressed in British Pounds).  The will was probated October, 1802
