2 CONT # Marriage Source:  Jacob Dirksen&apos;s Diary records from New Home ND. See www. DakotaDirksens. com
2 CONT # Notes: His descendants emigrated to South Dakota and spelled their last name &quot;Dirksen&quot;. Although some researchers have suggested he is an ancestor of U.S. Sen. Everett McKinley Dirksen, the Senator&apos;s own books link him to Volga Ger
2 CONC mans who immigrated to Indiana. In the 1835 census, Heinrich is listed at Alexanderthal #11, the home of his father Johann K. Duerksen, who emigrated (with Elder Goertz group of 179 families) from Tragheimerweide, Prussia in 1819 with his wife Kath
2 CONC arina, sons Johann J. &quot;Oel-Ohm&quot;, Heinrich J. and daughter Eva, who died before 1835. Heinrich and his wife died in Alexanderthal. All of their children emigrated to Dakota Territory where they became Seventh Day Adventists and spelled the
2 CONC ir last name &quot;Dirksen&quot;. His brother Johann&apos;s children went to Kansas and spelled their name Duerksen. Four of Heinrich&apos;s children (Jacob, Abraham, Cornelius and Eva Guenther) immigrated 28 Jul 1876 SS Vaderland, Philadelphia. Th
2 CONC en Elizabeth came also to Dakota Territory in 1878 and Johann in 1885.
